# Every text file is LF, in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# ⛔ WHY THIS EXISTS, AND WHY eol=lf RATHER THAN text=auto ALONE (2026-11-22).
#
# The generators hash file bytes. build.py derives the styles.css cache-buster
# from the contents of styles.css, and every sitemap_state.json sha256 from the
# contents of the finished page. Python's text-mode open(..., "w") writes \r\n
# on Windows, and a CRLF checkout makes those hashes come out different from
# everyone else's.
#
# Run on the Gateway without this file, build.py produced
# styles.css?v=ca1580d291 — the hash of the 76,487-byte CRLF copy — where the
# Mac and CI both produce 7898ff8449 for the 75,541-byte file. Every page went
# out pointing at a stylesheet version no other machine agrees with, and every
# sitemap hash was computed over the wrong bytes. test.yml's convergence step
# went red three times before the cause was understood, and the repair took a
# rebuild on ubuntu through season.yml.
#
# text=auto alone normalises what is COMMITTED. That is not enough here: the
# generators read the WORKING TREE, so the checkout has to be LF too, which is
# what eol=lf adds. core.autocrlf on the machine no longer matters either way.
#
# ⚠️ Windows is safer than it was, but season.yml is still the way to
# rebuild. Python writes \r\n there, so generated pages land CRLF in the
# working tree and git normalises them on commit: the committed bytes are
# right. The hashes read off that CRLF working tree used to be wrong, and
# that half is fixed as of 2026-11-24. Every byte hash in the build is now
# platform stable: build.py _digest() normalises line endings before hashing
# a page, and the only other two (CSS_V in build.py and books.py) read
# styles.css, which is not generated, so eol=lf keeps it LF everywhere. A
# Windows build no longer stamps today's date on pages nobody touched. What
# has not changed is everything else below. Rebuild through
# `gh workflow run season.yml` instead, and treat a second run printing
# "No change today." as the proof it converged. Note season.yml pushes with
# GITHUB_TOKEN, so it does NOT trigger test.yml, and it does not run
# make_publish.py or make_progress.py — /publish/, /reviews/, /links/,
# /progress/ and /support/ are not rebuilt by it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never normalised. Covers everything committed here that is not text:
# 370 jpg, 244 webp, 47 png, 9 m4a, 7 mp4, 2 pdf, 2 epub.
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png  binary
*.webp binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.epub binary
*.m4a  binary
*.mp3  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.mov  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary

# .svg is XML and stays text, so it normalises like any other source file.
